\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Choosing a turn at opposite momenta}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On an axial spin field the same transverse rotation fixes
each of two opposite momenta in \ref{fdip-016Y}. Measuring a
turn from the other end of the axis can exchange the rotation
and its inverse. Conjugating the field coefficients can also
invert a rotation eigenvalue. Which two operations enter the
comparison of degrees?}
